-- title:
--   Bounded triangle and pause moves on finite vertex rows
-- statement:
--   Let $V$ have decidable equality, let $\mathcal F$ be a predicate on finite vertex sets, and let $B\in\mathbb N$. Bounded triangle-row equivalence is generated by
--   $$p[a,b,c]s\longleftrightarrow p[a,c]s\quad(\{a,b,c\}\in\mathcal F),\qquad
--   p[a,a]s\longleftrightarrow p[a]s,$$
--   together with reflexivity, symmetry, and transitivity, requiring every displayed row to have length at most $B$. Enlarging $B$ preserves the relation; adjoining fixed prefix and suffix rows increases the bound by their lengths. A fan chain based at $u$ has consecutive triangles $\{u,v_j,v_{j+1}\}\in\mathcal F$. It contracts the row $[u,v_0,\ldots,v_n]$ to $[u,v_n]$ without increasing its length bound.
-- source:
--   Ruijun Wang, Continuous graph homomorphisms of higher dimensional abelian group actions, arXiv:2609.39824v1 (30 September 2026), Sections 2–7, supporting construction for Theorem 1.4 and Proposition 7.1; https://arxiv.org/html/2609.39824v1. Formalization-specific infrastructure in the import closure; individual helper assertions are not represented as separately numbered paper theorems. Original Lean module AbelianTargets/TriangleRowMoves.lean, selected declaration lines 7-18, 20-28, 30-48, 50-54, 56-69; SHA-256 662cb3fd499c1de2db459b446a7e3b23cfd25558e11f1b218b0581fc4568924f. Selected spans are from the final generated manifest. The original source snapshot is local; no public repository URL or commit was available.

